  "p. 26 n. 1: Read [D21 over Z1] [Q3 over N35] re pen, \"this chapter\"? (signs: D21, Z1, Q3, N35); reference mark is the superscript 1 after pu (Rubric LXXII line 1)"
 ],
 "notes": "Section XXII runs p.25 row1 to p.26 'nebṭet ḳerḥ' (line 10); Rubric LXXII from 'Àr' (p.26, before its numeral 1.) to p.27 'àu Àusàr ān Ani' (line 7); stopped above PLATE VII. Numerals falling inside hyphenated units (àu - à / 2., erṭāu - nà / 3., Re - stau / 5., āχem - nà / 7.) were split at the numeral; numerals inside unhyphenated words (samau / 8., Ṭeṭṭeṭ / 5.) kept the word whole at the line where it begins and noted. p.25 star before '4.' and p.27 star after '7.' taken as N14 of ṭuat; p.27 O49 after '5.' taken as det of Ṭeṭṭeṭ. Rubric overlines: p.25 row1 (Re…en), row2 (nef, em, Neter-χert), row7 (ī-nà…àb-à), row8 (em…nà); p.26 row3 (ṭā-k…àm-f), all three rubric rows of LXXII except Àr; p.27 rows1 (to ent; not Àusàr), 2, 3, 4 all, row5 except neteru, row6 ḥeḥ en sep only. Printer's signature 'E' at foot of p.25 and 'E 2' at foot of p.27 ignored. Several sign identifications are approximations (see approx/unsure)."
